# Media Library menu (mod22, MedialibWin): 11 entries.
#
# The menu draws and dispatches from a table of 6-byte entries
# {u16 0, u16 string id, u16 type} (stock: 8 entries at 0x0300e6bc, count
# hard-coded). The dispatcher (FUN_0307957c) is called with the type of the
# entry under the cursor; for types 1/3/4/5 it takes the browser window title
# from title_table[type], and returning from the browser restores the cursor
# from MusicTypeSelID (library_menu_42_mod22_restore.S maps it to a position).
#
# New table in unused zeros of mod22 data (0x0300e708..0x0300e8a7):
#   pos 0 Now Playing (0x59, 0)    6 Albums (0x5c, 4)
#       1 All Songs (0x5a, 1)      7 Genres (0x5d, 5)
#       2 Favorites (0x61, 2)      8 Folder Navigation (0x5f, 0xa)
#       3 Most Played (0x84, 8)    9 Recent Albums (0x87, 7)
#       4 Artists (0x85, 9)       10 Media Library Refresh (0x62, 6)
#       5 Album Artists (0x86, 3)
# Types 7, 8, and 9 are handled by library_menu_40.
22:0300e708:0000 5900 0000  0000 5a00 0100  0000 6100 0200  0000 8400 0800  0000 8500 0900
22:0300e726:0000 8600 0300  0000 5c00 0400  0000 5d00 0500  0000 5f00 0a00  0000 8700 0700  0000 6200 0600

# Draw and dispatch use the new table (literal-pool pointers). Titles keep
# the stock table (0x030799e8 unchanged), which is indexed by type.
22:03079e74:08e70003
22:0307a2f4:08e70003

# Stock Artists groups by album artist (mod39 copies ALBUMARTIST over ARTIST):
# title it "Album Artists" (stock table row 3 string id).
22:0300e6d0:8600

# Item count 8 -> 11.
22:030794f4:0b21                # movs r1, #11   (menu state +0)
22:03079560:c1f10b00            # rsb.w r0, r1, #11

